# Declared prefixes take their names first. The undeclared .../org# falls back to "org" and gets
# -2; the two undeclared .../thing# take "thing" and "thing-2" in sorted IRI order; and Ex: and ex:
# would be one file on a case-insensitive filesystem, so the later IRI gets -2.
@prefix org: <http://example.org/mine#> .
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/lower#> .
@prefix Ex: <http://example.org/upper#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

org:Mine a owl:Class .
ex:Lower a owl:Class .
Ex:Upper a owl:Class .
<http://example.org/org#Theirs> a owl:Class .
<http://b.example/thing#B> a owl:Class .
<http://a.example/thing#A> a owl:Class .
